caption: Vampire Field Manual — 🧛 Field Identification & Known Weaknesses
campaign-component: field-identification-known-weaknesses

“If it looks hungry, sounds poetic, and shows up after sunset — assume vampire until proven otherwise.”
 — Trainer’s Handbook, Vol. 3: Things That Glitter and Bite

Across recorded encounters (11,472 cases, per Q4 report), the following vulnerabilities have been observed with inconsistent frequency:

Weakness

Frequency

Notes

Fire

87%

Always a safe bet. HR-approved for open use outdoors.

Sunlight

74%

Variants may resist or delay burn. Never assume.

Holy Symbols / Faith Magic

63%

Must be actively believed in by wielder. Faith outsourcing not reimbursable.

Silver

58%

Ineffective against purely arcane variants. Still looks classy.

Wood (natural, untreated)

41%

Stakes, arrows, or clubs; IKEA furniture doesn’t count.

Running Water

27%

Results vary by planet. Test cautiously.

Garlic

18%

Works, but only as social deterrent.

Counting Compulsion (rice, salt, etc.)

<1%

Rare, but always funny when it works.

Bureaucracy

100%

All vampires universally despise paperwork. Use Form 6-V tactically.
